hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1581","Narrated by Muammal bin Hisham Al-Yashkari, on the authority of Ismail, meaning Ibn Aliya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq. H Al-Fadl bin Yaqoub Al-Jazari narrated to us, Abdul-Ala narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us. H Sa’id bin Yahya bin Sa’id al-Umayyad narrated to us, my father, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, and Muhammad bin Rafi’ and Ya’qub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi, they said: Yazid told us, and he is the son of Harun, Muhammad told us, and he is the son of Ishaq, Makhoul told me, on the authority of Mahmoud Ibn al-Rabi’ al-Ansari, who lived in Ilya, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the morning prayer with us. The recitation became difficult for him, so when he left, he said: “I see you reciting behind your imam?” He said: We said: Yes, by God, O Messenger of God. This man said: “Do not do so except according to the Mother of the Book, for there is no prayer for one who does not recite it.” This is the hadith of Ibn Ulayya and Abd al-A’la."
